			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4184191">
									

<p>Alright, finished up with school stuff, can now proceed to talk a bit more about the SCP! First off, I will be doing a bit of a bit of revisioning once JamCon ends. The article was written in a rush because JamCon so some things are a little rushed, could stand to be cleaned up a bit (the history section in particular was /really/ last minute and could stand to be a bit more cohesive and punchier)</p>
<p>The main intent with this article an object that compelled you to do horrible things not through some memetic/compulsive/mind affecting in general effect, but through application of psychological principles.</p>
<p>For example, people are more inclined to do further somethings for someone (and begin to regard them as trustworthy and good) if they do even a small thing for that someone first. The Benjamin Franklin effect, since the lad used it to make political opponents come to like him @ having them do small favors for him. That's why the first trial, walking a thousand miles, is something you'll complete/do for the box even if you don't want to. You literally can't help but starting the trials, you literally can't help but doing something for the box. From there, it has a wedge in you, and increasingly uses various means of reinforcement to keep you doing the trials &quot;you can't stop now you've already started&quot; &quot;what's one more&quot; &quot;I believe in you&quot; &quot;what you've done will be meaningless if you don't keep going&quot;</p>
<p>It's the exact sort of stuff that can make cults commit mass suicide irl @ refuse to believe in reality and further and further justify their delusions because they've sacrificed/come this far/need to finish what they've started/have been positively reinforced etc., so it's actually entirely realistic a guy would go this far for an object that's shown itself to have some anomalous properties</p>
<p><span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sidewindered" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2949374); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2949374&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1552557410" alt="Sidewindered" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2949374)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sidewindered" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2949374); return false;">Sidewindered</a></span> and <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/fuelboy" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5197941); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5197941&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1552557410" alt="FuelBoy" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5197941)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/fuelboy" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5197941); return false;">FuelBoy</a></span> Thank you very much for the positive comments ! They mean a lot !</p>
<p><span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/modernmajorgeneral" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(274283); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=274283&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1552557410" alt="ModernMajorGeneral" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=274283)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/modernmajorgeneral" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(274283); return false;">ModernMajorGeneral</a></span> Thank you greatly for the crit; I'll be fixing that one error, and I definitely might change the shark punching ref ! I'll also definitely take the order of description into consideration.</p>
<p>Funnily enough, it's not actually /cursed/ in one sense. It genuinely would have granted the guy's super conscious desire, it's just a stupid ass in one sense box for all its psychological manipulation and it genuinely innocently prioritized the guy's hongry over his conscious wants. If he hadn't been hongry it might have all been worth it; the senselessness of it all was why I felt real Shaggy dog hours.</p>
<p><span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/shaggydredlocks" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1722371); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1722371&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1552557410" alt="Shaggydredlocks" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1722371)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/shaggydredlocks" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1722371); return false;">Shaggydredlocks</a></span> Thank you so much for the praise and I'm glad you enjoyed reading ! That honestly is a pretty good idea and I'll definitely look into it for the revision !</p>

							</div>

								
					
